{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'gh issue view 7 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --comments && git show --format=fuller --no-ext-diff 3ec72dc -- && git diff --name-only HEAD..origin/issue-7-phase-1-analysis-foundation-vgt-sidecar && git log --left-right --graph --oneline HEAD...origin/issue-7-phase-1-analysis-foundation-vgt-sidecar'","aggregated_output":"author:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 1: no reviewer comment was left on the issue/PR to work from (checked issue comments, PR comments, and PR reviews — all empty), so I reviewed the implementation against the acceptance criteria myself.\n\nFound and fixed a real bug: `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`'s `write_settings` unconditionally rewrote the sidecar as `schema_version: 1` on every apply/re-apply, silently deleting any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written. Since the `.vgt` sidecar is meant to be the single shared contract between the ReaScript apply action and the Python analysis CLI, re-applying Phase 0 (e.g. to switch the reference track) was destroying analysis work already done — the reader/writer sides of the contract weren't actually symmetric.\n\nFix: the action now reads back any existing `analysis` object before overwriting the sidecar and round-trips it verbatim, only advancing `schema_version` to 2 once analysis exists (a fresh apply with no prior analysis still writes schema 1, so the existing Phase 0 live-verification procedure is unaffected). Verified the Lua brace-balancing extraction logic against nested-object JSON with a standalone interpreter, and confirmed the resulting output is valid JSON in both the with- and without-analysis cases.\n\nAll 13 existing tests still pass; this is a REAPER-only code path so it isn't covered by the Python test suite (same limitation as the rest of the Lua apply action).\n--\ncommit 3ec72dc64abf108adb9858942025397147abc5f0\nAuthor:     Marek Kucharski <marekkucharski@mini.local>\nAuthorDate: Sat Jul 18 13:58:41 2026 +0200\nCommit:     Marek Kucharski <marekkucharski@mini.local>\nCommitDate: Sat Jul 18 13:58:41 2026 +0200\n\n    fix: preserve analysis block across Phase 0 re-apply\n    \n    The ReaScript apply action unconditionally rewrote the sidecar as\n    schema_version 1 on every run, silently deleting any `analysis` block\n    `vgt analyze` had already written. Since the sidecar is the single\n    shared contract between the DAW action and the Python CLI, re-applying\n    Phase 0 (e.g. to pick a different reference track) was destroying\n    analysis work. The action now reads back and round-trips any existing\n    `analysis` object, only advancing schema_version to 2 once one exists.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 1912cce..0a2f734 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@ The action is intentionally the mutation path: it uses REAPER's API and never te\n - pops up a menu of the project's own (non-`[vgt]`) tracks and asks which one is the **reference** to mirror;\n - creates a REAPER folder named `[vgt] <reference track name>` (e.g. `[vgt] The Seven Rivers (Full March - 3_00)`) with a `[vgt] Mirror` child;\n - clones only the chosen reference track's file-backed media to the mirror track, without adding sends, changing source tracks, or changing project tempo/sample rate;\n-- writes the adjacent `.vgt` sidecar — named after the project, e.g. `Reaper Project.vgt` — with schema version 1, its two created track GUIDs, and config recording the reference track;\n-- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in the sidecar **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area.\n+- writes the adjacent `.vgt` sidecar — named after the project, e.g. `Reaper Project.vgt` — with its two created track GUIDs and config recording the reference track;\n+- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in the sidecar **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area, carrying forward any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written (schema stays version 1 until analysis exists, then becomes version 2).\n \n The folder/mirror are therefore idempotent and original tracks remain untouched. REAPER-native click-source items have no file to clone, so choosing a click track mirrors nothing. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n \ndiff --git a/reascript/vgt_initialize.lua b/reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\nindex a965292..7e59eb0 100644\n--- a/reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\n+++ b/reascript/vgt_initialize.lua\n@@ -68,11 +68,17 @@ local function choose_reference(candidates)\n   return candidates[choice]\n end\n \n-local function read_managed_guids()\n+local function read_sidecar_body()\n   local file = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"r\")\n-  if not file then return {} end\n+  if not file then return nil end\n   local body = file:read(\"*a\")\n   file:close()\n+  return body\n+end\n+\n+local function read_managed_guids()\n+  local body = read_sidecar_body()\n+  if not body then return {} end\n   local guids = {}\n   -- GUIDs are deliberately read only from our schema's managed_track_guids array.\n   local array = body:match('\"managed_track_guids\"%s*:%s*%[(.-)%]') or \"\"\n@@ -80,6 +86,29 @@ local function read_managed_guids()\n   return guids\n end\n \n+-- The Python `vgt analyze` stage (schema v2) adds a top-level \"analysis\"\n+-- object to the sidecar. This action is the sole writer of the sidecar's\n+-- other fields, so it must round-trip that object verbatim on re-apply\n+-- rather than silently dropping any analysis a user has already run.\n+local function read_analysis_block()\n+  local body = read_sidecar_body()\n+  if not body then return nil end\n+  local key_start = body:find('\"analysis\"%s*:%s*{')\n+  if not key_start then return nil end\n+  local brace_start = body:find(\"{\", key_start)\n+  local depth = 0\n+  for index = brace_start, #body do\n+    local char = body:sub(index, index)\n+    if char == \"{\" then\n+      depth = depth + 1\n+    elseif char == \"}\" then\n+      depth = depth - 1\n+      if depth == 0 then return body:sub(brace_start, index) end\n+    end\n+  end\n+  return nil\n+end\n+\n local function remove_previous_managed_tracks()\n   local managed = read_managed_guids()\n   -- A GUID in the sidecar alone is not enough: preserve any track whose current name is not vgt-owned.\n@@ -124,14 +153,22 @@ local function copy_file_backed_items(source, destination)\n end\n \n local function write_settings(folder, mirror, reference)\n+  -- Preserve any analysis the Python CLI already wrote (schema v2); a fresh\n+  -- sidecar with no prior analysis stays schema v1, matching Phase 0's\n+  -- long-standing on-disk format.\n+  local analysis = read_analysis_block()\n+  local schema_version = analysis and 2 or 1\n+  local analysis_field = analysis and ('\\n  \"analysis\": ' .. analysis .. \",\") or \"\"\n+\n   local file, error_message = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"w\")\n   if not file then error(error_message) end\n   file:write(string.format([[{\n-  \"schema_version\": 1,\n+  \"schema_version\": %d,%s\n   \"managed_track_guids\": [\"%s\", \"%s\"],\n   \"config\": {\"reference_track_name\": \"%s\", \"reference_track_guid\": \"%s\", \"folder_name\": \"%s\", \"mirror_name\": \"%s\"}\n }\n ]],\n+    schema_version, analysis_field,\n     reaper.GetTrackGUID(folder), reaper.GetTrackGUID(mirror),\n     escaped(track_name(reference)), reaper.GetTrackGUID(reference),\n     escaped(PREFIX .. \" \" .. track_name(reference)), escaped(MIRROR_NAME)))\n.pm/log.ndjson\n.pm/runs/issue-7-start-20260718T115011Z.log\n.pm/runs/issue-7-start-20260718T115333Z.log\n.pm/runs/issue-7-start-20260718T115446Z.log\n.pm/runs/issue-7-start-20260718T115911Z.log\n.pm/state.json\nREADME.md\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua\nsrc/vgt/__init__.py\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py\nsrc/vgt/cli.py\nsrc/vgt/project.py\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py\ntests/test_analysis.py\n< 31905d9 chore(pm): start review issue #7 (codex)\n< a6834b0 chore(pm): start fix issue #7 (claude)\n< c537162 chore(pm): start review issue #7 (codex)\n> 3ec72dc fix: preserve analysis block across Phase 0 re-apply\n> 434a9c9 docs: document vgt analyze and the corrections mechanism\n> ccda5d5 feat: add vgt analyze CLI stage and .vgt sidecar schema v2\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
